      "rationale": "The ledger clip explicitly states insertion between aa 154\u2013155 of full-length TSPAN2, placing the junction squarely within the large extracellular loop (LEL, topology landmarks 111\u2013185). Python verification confirms residue 154 = K and residue 155 = E, both 44 and 31 residues from the flanking TM boundaries respectively, well clear of the \u22653-residue minimum. The nearest conserved CCG-motif cysteines (C151, C152) are 2\u20133 residues upstream of the junction; the paper nonetheless validated this exact position in the intact membrane-anchored protein, so the site is accepted as published. No residue-identity mismatch was found. Full-length, membrane-anchored TSPAN2 with ABD or P19 heterologous peptides inserted between residues 154 and 155 in the large extracellular loop (LEL, residues 111\u2013185). Construct expressed in mammalian cells as an intact transmembrane protein.",
